Rice Leaf Disease Detection Using CNN

Project Overview

This project focuses on detecting rice leaf diseases using Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN). The model is trained using rice leaf images to classify different types of diseases.

Objectives

- To identify rice leaf diseases using image classification.
- To build a CNN deep learning model.
- To train and evaluate the model using image datasets.
- To predict rice leaf disease from input images.

Dataset

The dataset contains three classes of rice leaf diseases:

- Brown Spot – 40 images
- Bacterial Leaf Blight – 40 images
- Leaf Smut – 39 images

Total Images: 119

Technologies Used

- Python
- TensorFlow
- Keras
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- CNN (Convolutional Neural Network)
- Jupyter Notebook

Project Workflow

1. Import required libraries.
2. Load the rice leaf image dataset.
3. Extract and organize the dataset.
4. Preprocess the images.
5. Split the dataset into training and validation sets.
6. Build the CNN model.
7. Train the model for 10 epochs.
8. Evaluate the model.
9. Visualize training and validation accuracy.
10. Save the trained model.

Model

A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is used to classify rice leaf diseases based on image features.

Disease Classes

1. Brown Spot
2. Bacterial Leaf Blight
3. Leaf Smut

Results

The model was trained for 10 epochs. Training accuracy, validation accuracy, and validation loss were evaluated.

Output

The project generates disease classification results based on the input rice leaf images.

Conclusion

This project demonstrates how deep learning and CNN can be used for rice leaf disease classification. It helps in identifying different rice leaf diseases through image processing.

